{"pages": [{"id": 527658, "key": "Shoshoni_language", "title": "Shoshoni language", "excerpt": "and <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span> (/ʃoʊˈʃoʊni/, shoh-SHOH-nee; Shoshoni orthography: Sosoni&#039; ta̲i̲kwappe, newe ta̲i̲kwappe or neme ta̲i̲kwappeh), is a Uto-Aztecan <span class=\"searchmatch\">language</span> from", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Uto-Aztecan language spoken in western US", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/svg+xml", "width": 60, "height": 38, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Shoshone_map.svg/60px-Shoshone_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 544742, "key": "Shoshone", "title": "Shoshone", "excerpt": "traditionally speak the Shoshoni <span class=\"searchmatch\">language</span>, part of the Numic <span class=\"searchmatch\">languages</span> branch of the large Uto-Aztecan <span class=\"searchmatch\">language</span> family. The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span> were sometimes called the", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Native American tribe", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/png", "width": 60, "height": 46, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Shoshone_group_American_Indian_Mongoloid.png/60px-Shoshone_group_American_Indian_Mongoloid.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 2055841, "key": "Western_Shoshone", "title": "Western Shoshone", "excerpt": "<span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">language</span>. Other <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span>-speaking groups include the Goshute (Utah-Nevada border), Northern <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span> (southern Idaho), and Eastern <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span> (western", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Grouping of Shoshone tribes in the Great Basin of the U.S.", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/png", "width": 60, "height": 45, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Carrie%26MaryDann.png/60px-Carrie%26MaryDann.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 26516977, "key": "Lemhi_Shoshone", "title": "Lemhi Shoshone", "excerpt": "The Lemhi <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span> are a tribe of Northern <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span>, also called the Akaitikka, Agaidika, or &quot;Eaters of Salmon&quot;. The name &quot;Lemhi&quot; comes from Fort Lemhi", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Tribe of Northern Shoshone", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 83, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Native_Americans_from_Southeastern_Idaho%2C_Lemhi._Chief._Tindoor_-_NARA_-_519297.jpg/60px-Native_Americans_from_Southeastern_Idaho%2C_Lemhi._Chief._Tindoor_-_NARA_-_519297.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 25448700, "key": "Eastern_Shoshone", "title": "Eastern Shoshone", "excerpt": "Eastern <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span> are <span class=\"searchmatch\">Shoshone</span> who primarily live in Wyoming and in the northeast corner of the Great Basin where Utah, Idaho and Wyoming meet and are", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Native American tribe in Wyoming", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 91, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Washakie_%28Shoots-the-Buffalo-Running%29%2C_a_Shoshoni_chief%2C_half-length%2C_seated%2C_holding_pipe_-_NARA_-_530875.jpg/60px-Washakie_%28Shoots-the-Buffalo-Running%29%2C_a_Shoshoni_chief%2C_half-length%2C_seated%2C_holding_pipe_-_NARA_-_530875.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 38040232, "key": "Northern_Shoshone", "title": "Northern Shoshone", "excerpt": "I